       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and I don't know of any indication that calls for five times the labeled maximum. An overdose of this size can cause profound, prolonged hypotension and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and it can be hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose, if that works for you.\n- **Enter 5 mg** by mouth once daily.\n- **Route the 50 mg order through pharmacy or your institution's high-dose override process.** If a specialist or protocol really does call for this dose, a pharmacist or attending can verify it and place it with documentation. If you give me the rationale, I can help you draft it.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter 5 mg or 10 mg."
